<title>GERMANY: Waigel says seeks broad spend cuts, not tax hikes.</title>
<headline>Waigel says seeks broad spend cuts, not tax hikes.</headline>
<dateline>SCHWABMUENCHEN, Germany 1997-06-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel on Saturday heralded further spending cuts in all possible areas for the 1998 budget.</p>
<p>At a meeting of the Christian Social Union (CSU) party, Waigel said tax increases were &quot;not a good instrument and not good for the economy&quot; and were also impossible to push through politically.</p>
<p>Radical savings were the only alternative, Waigel said, and all areas would have to contribute.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
